CloudBurrow patch 51 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1487). Applies after patch 0047; needs patch
0044.

Patch 0044 gave the engine a clock, the system's moved forward by the
offset CloudBurrow's front sets when it advances its own, and
CURRENT_TIMESTAMP() and the change times read it; but the catalog still
stamped a table's, view's and function's creation and update times by
the system clock, so INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES' creation_time read
another clock than CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(), as did the year a CAST ... FORMAT
without one defaults to and UNIX_TIMESTAMP(). The patch reads the
engine's clock there too (the catalog's sync time with them, so that the
catalog still finds each update), and adds googlesqlite.Now, that clock,
which bigquery-emulator patch 0041 stamps the times it reports by.
clock_times_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

